{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>וילפת</b>. From the nif'al stem, like 'their paths are warped' (Job 24:13). And the meaning is 'was twisted.' So too 'Samson turned' (Judges 16:30). It is not like <i>mesos</i>. And the matter is that he turned from side to side." "<b>והנה אשה</b>. It is possible that she said to him, 'Do not fear,' and a woman's voice is always recognizable. Or the moonlight was abundant and he saw that she had no beard, and he could also recognize her by her garments."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites a form he transliterates as משוש; likely referring to a proposed alternative root or a reading tradition; rendered as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:31.720146421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}